[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Italian Game"]
[Variation "Rousseau Gambit, 4.Nc3"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "gambit,tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "fork,hanging-piece"]
[Themes "pawn-grab,open-f-file"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "4.Nc3"]
[Start "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5"]

4. Nc3 $2 { Defends e4 with a piece, but fxe4 then wins a pawn and hits the knight on f3. } 4... fxe4 { Takes the pawn. White's knight on f3 is attacked, and the bishop on c4 has to watch out too. } 5. Bxg8 ( 5. Nxe4 $2 d5 { Hits the bishop and the knight on e4 at once; White loses a piece. } 6. Bd3 dxe4 7. Bxe4 ) 5... exf3 { Takes the knight in return. Black is a pawn up and White's king is without its knight. } 6. Bd5 fxg2 { Takes another pawn and attacks the rook on h1. } 7. Bxg2 d6 { Frees the bishop and keeps e5 solid. Black has the extra pawn. Plan: complete development with ...Be7 and ...Nf6, and keep the extra pawn safe. } *
